{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short --untracked-files=all && git branch --show-current && git log --oneline main..HEAD && rg -n '\"'^#{1,3} '\"' docs/plans/2026-08-28-1433-feat-capitalize-words-plan.md && sed -n '1,220p' docs/plans/2026-08-28-1433-feat-capitalize-words-plan.md && rg -n \\\"capitalize_words|capitalize\\\\(\\\" toolkit tests\"","aggregated_output":"?? docs/plans/2026-08-28-1433-feat-capitalize-words-plan.md\nrelay/T-6\n11:## Goal Capsule\n20:## Product Contract\n22:### Summary\n27:### Problem Frame\n32:### Requirements\n38:### Scope Boundaries\n45:## Planning Contract\n47:### Key Technical Decisions\n51:### Assumptions\n57:## Implementation Units\n59:### U1. Add the word-capitalization helper and coverage\n77:## Verification Contract\n83:## Definition of Done\n---\ntitle: Capitalize Words Helper - Plan\ntype: feat\ndate: 2026-08-28\nartifact_contract: ce-unified-plan/v1\nartifact_readiness: implementation-ready\nproduct_contract_source: ce-plan-bootstrap\nexecution: code\n---\n\n## Goal Capsule\n\n- **Objective:** Callers can normalize a phrase into title-style words with predictable casing and spacing.\n- **Means:** Add a small whitespace-tokenizing helper beside the existing text helpers (KTD1).\n- **Authority hierarchy:** This plan defines the requested behavior. Existing helpers and unittest coverage define local style.\n- **Stop conditions:** The helper matches all requested casing examples, collapses whitespace when joining words, and the unittest suite passes.\n- **Execution profile:** Single-session, single-unit implementation.\n- **Tail ownership:** The implementing session commits the helper, its tests, and this plan on `relay/T-6`.\n\n## Product Contract\n\n### Summary\n\nAdd `capitalize_words(text)` as a public helper in `toolkit/text.py`.\nIt converts each whitespace-delimited word to an uppercase first character followed by lowercase remaining characters, then joins words with one space.\n\n### Problem Frame\n\nThe toolkit has small, reusable text transformations but no helper for consistently formatted words.\nCallers would otherwise have to repeat casing and whitespace normalization logic.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- R1. `capitalize_words(text)` splits the input on whitespace and joins the resulting words with a single space.\n- R2. Each output word has its first character capitalized and every remaining character lowercased.\n- R3. Coverage proves the helper for a lowercase phrase, an already-capitalized phrase, and an all-caps phrase.\n\n### Scope Boundaries\n\n- The helper does not preserve original whitespace runs.\n- The helper does not add a broader text-formatting API or modify existing helpers.\n\n---\n\n## Planning Contract\n\n### Key Technical Decisions\n\n- KTD1. **Use the language's word-casing operation after whitespace splitting.** This directly expresses R1 and R2 while matching the repository's preference for small standard-library helpers.\n\n### Assumptions\n\n- Python's default whitespace splitting is the intended interpretation of \"split on whitespace.\"\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Units\n\n### U1. Add the word-capitalization helper and coverage\n\n- **Goal:** Provide `capitalize_words(text)` and prove its requested casing behavior.\n- **Requirements:** R1, R2, R3\n- **Dependencies:** None.\n- **Files:**\n  - `toolkit/text.py`\n  - `tests/test_text.py`\n- **Approach:** Add the helper alongside the existing public text functions. Split the input into words, apply the standard word-casing operation to each token, and join the results using one literal space.\n- **Patterns to follow:** Follow the existing concise function docstrings in `toolkit/text.py` and the one-assertion unittest methods in `tests/test_text.py`.\n- **Test scenarios:**\n  - A lowercase phrase such as `\"hello world\"` becomes `\"Hello World\"`.\n  - An already-capitalized phrase such as `\"Hello World\"` remains `\"Hello World\"`.\n  - An all-caps phrase such as `\"HELLO WORLD\"` becomes `\"Hello World\"`.\n- **Verification:** The full unittest suite passes with the new helper and the existing text helpers unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Contract\n\n| Command | Applies to | Done signal |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `python -m unittest discover` | U1 and repository gate | The complete unittest suite reports success. |\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- `toolkit/text.py` exports `capitalize_words(text)` with the R1 and R2 behavior.\n- `tests/test_text.py` contains the three requested phrase-casing scenarios.\n- `python -m unittest discover` passes.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
